+// Delay for the specified number of microseconds after the OPL
+// subsystem is initialized.
+//
+// The stock implementation schedules a callback and blocks on an SDL
+// condvar until the (separate) audio thread renders far enough to fire
+// it. PureDarwin's driver is single-threaded pull - there is no audio
+// thread to make progress while we block, so instead the driver advances
+// the emulated clock synchronously (rendering into a scratch buffer and
+// firing any due callbacks along the way).
 
-// Delay for specified number of microseconds after OPL subsystem is initialized
